{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/25726-what-s-in-your-game-room","id":25726,"title":"What's in your Game Room?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-08T03:49:15-08:00","id":25726,"title":"What's in your Game Room?","content":"I started a thread before called What's on your game table and got many responses about how much or how little STs have at their tables come game time. It was suggested that asking about people's Game rooms would yield a whole different response so that's what I've come here to ask.<br /> <br /> I'll start off by saying right now, My game (Dining) room sucks. I have no Table for Table top. I need to get a new one. The book case of Booze and RPG books is all discombobulated and all my game books are in stacks and I can't see or reach the ones I want without knocking over massive towers I don't want to have to stack back up again. I'm just not set up for running any games and that makes me a sad flower.<br /> <br /> Ideally I would have a table that can seat 4-6 and enough room for maybe 2 large bookshelves to properly house all my Books (and all booze). The second fridge would be nearby for beverages and refreshments. I would have a crockpot in the kitchen for making tasty food all the players can share. If needed but not necessary i would have the stereo set up on the kitchen counter that I can cue music with. I might even invest in a tablet for the PDFs I don't have and an image search should I need them since everyone tells me how awesome they are. Lastly beneath the table I would have a rolling container for all the game supplies to be stored in when not needed.<br /> <br /> If I wanted to get really fancy I'd have my games at my work place after hours where I can use one of their AV conference rooms with the big screen to load any images or maps, play music or even conference video call over Skype to have more players from other places play with us. Could even use the markers and white board for our maps and notes. That'd be Sweeeeet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T04:52:18-08:00","id":25737,"title":"","content":"My game room doesn't exist at all right now. once I'm settled into a house, I'll probably have a decent enough gaming table, my books on the shelves, and a halfway decent place to run some rpgs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/238-hammerofheaven","name":"HammerofHeaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar238_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}